"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JYGSV7SE1S03PH9\",\"title\":\"Varhad Industrial Cotton Stalk Biochar Project — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Varhad Industrial Cotton Stalk Biochar Project\",\"Varhad\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2027\",\"Project code\",\"GBQA\",\"PROTOCOL DETAILS\",\"Current protocol version\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"GBQA\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"08 Aug 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"07 Jul 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://varhad.in\",\"t\":\"Varhad\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JJP6BWF51S05RE8\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JJP6BWF51S05RE8/prj_1JYGSV7SE1S03PH9/pjd_1K2FJGZCW1S07HQ5/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JJP6BWF51S05RE8/prj_1JYGSV7SE1S03PH9/pjd_1JZJSMBYK1S07N7A/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nVarhad Industrial Cotton Stalk Biochar Project\\nVarhad\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2027\\nProject code\\nGBQA\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nThe Varhad Indistrial Cotton Stalk (VICOS) project involves setting up industrial biochar pyrolysis reactors in the Vidarbha region of Maharashtra for the purpose of converting agri waste in the form of cotton stalk into biochar. This biochar is then mixed with organically produced compost at the same location to produce enriched blended biochar (called Biochaar++) for application in agricultural soils.\\n\\nNagpur, India\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 05 Aug 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2027\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2027\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n08 Aug 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n07 Jul 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"